          {
            "name": "README.md",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "# 04 — Array to Pointer Decay\n\n## 🎯 Array Decay\nWhen passed to functions, array identifiers decay to a pointer to their first element (`T*`), losing size information.\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "example.c",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nvoid print_size(int arr[]) {\n    printf(\"Inside function sizeof(arr): %zu (Pointer size!)\\n\", sizeof(arr));\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int arr[10];\n    printf(\"In main sizeof(arr): %zu (40 bytes)\\n\", sizeof(arr));\n    print_size(arr);\n    return 0;\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "exercise",
            "type": "directory",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "starter.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "// TODO: Implement an array sum function that requires passing length explicitly.\n"
              },
              {
                "name": "solution.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint sum_array(const int* arr, size_t len) {\n    int sum = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < len; i++) sum += arr[i];\n    return sum;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int numbers[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};\n    printf(\"Sum: %d\\n\", sum_array(numbers, 5));\n    return 0;\n}\n"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
