        "name": "06-structs-unions-and-alignment",
        "type": "directory",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "README.md",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "# 06 — Struct Padding, Alignment & Unions\n\n## 🎯 Struct Padding\nCompilers insert invisible padding bytes so fields align with word boundaries.\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "example.c",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nstruct PackedData {\n    char a;\n    int b;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\nint main(void) {\n    printf(\"=== 06: Packed Struct ===\\n\");\n    printf(\"Packed Struct Size: %zu bytes (5 bytes!)\\n\", sizeof(struct PackedData));\n    return 0;\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "exercise",
            "type": "directory",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "starter.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "// TODO: Create a union 'IPAddress' representing an IPv4 address as 4 bytes or 1 uint32_t.\n"
              },
              {
                "name": "solution.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n\nunion IPAddress {\n    uint32_t full_address;\n    uint8_t octets[4];\n};\n\nint main(void) {\n    union IPAddress ip;\n    ip.octets[0] = 127;\n    ip.octets[1] = 0;\n    ip.octets[2] = 0;\n    ip.octets[3] = 1;\n    printf(\"IP as 32-bit integer: 0x%08X\\n\", ip.full_address);\n    return 0;\n}\n"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "07-bitwise-operations-and-masks",
        "type": "directory",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "README.md",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "# 07 — Bitwise Operations & Flag Masks\n\n## 🎯 Common Bit Operations\n- Set bit: `flags |= (1 << n)`\n- Clear bit: `flags &= ~(1 << n)`\n- Toggle bit: `flags ^= (1 << n)`\n- Test bit: `(flags & (1 << n)) != 0`\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "example.c",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n\n#define FLAG_READ    (1 << 0) // 0x01\n#define FLAG_WRITE   (1 << 1) // 0x02\n#define FLAG_EXECUTE (1 << 2) // 0x04\n\nint main(void) {\n    int permissions = FLAG_READ | FLAG_WRITE;\n    printf(\"Can read? %s\\n\", (permissions & FLAG_READ) ? \"Yes\" : \"No\");\n    printf(\"Can execute? %s\\n\", (permissions & FLAG_EXECUTE) ? \"Yes\" : \"No\");\n    return 0;\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "exercise",
            "type": "directory",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "starter.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "// TODO: Write a function to count set bits (popcount) in a uint32_t.\n"
              },
              {
                "name": "solution.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n\nint count_set_bits(uint32_t n) {\n    int count = 0;\n    while (n > 0) {\n        count += (n & 1);\n        n >>= 1;\n    }\n    return count;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    printf(\"Set bits in 0b1011 (11): %d\\n\", count_set_bits(11));\n    return 0;\n}\n"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "08-functions-and-function-pointers",
        "type": "directory",
