      {
        "name": "17-safe-c-best-practices",
        "type": "directory",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "README.md",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "# 17 — Defensive C Systems Engineering\n\n## 🎯 Cleanup Idioms\nUsing `goto cleanup` provides single-exit resource freeing without deep nested error checks.\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "example.c",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nint process(void) {\n    int* res1 = (int*)malloc(100);\n    int* res2 = (int*)malloc(100);\n    int status = 0;\n\n    if (!res1 || !res2) {\n        status = -1;\n        goto cleanup;\n    }\n\ncleanup:\n    free(res1);\n    free(res2);\n    return status;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    printf(\"Process status: %d\\n\", process());\n    return 0;\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "exercise",
            "type": "directory",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "starter.c",
