      {
        "name": "18-interview-questions-and-drills",
        "type": "directory",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "README.md",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "# 18 — High-Yield C Interview Questions & Master Drills\n\n## 🧠 Top 10 Gotchas\n1. **Dangling Pointers**: Accessing memory after calling `free()`.\n2. **Pointer Subtraction**: Valid only between pointers to elements of the same array.\n3. **Integer Promotion**: Small types (`char`, `short`) promoted to `int` in expressions.\n4. **Off-by-One in Strings**: Forgetting the `\\0` terminator space (`char[5]` cannot store \"hello\").\n5. **`sizeof` on Parameters**: Array parameters decay to pointer size.\n6. **Sequence Points**: Modifying variable twice in same expression is undefined (`i = i++`).\n7. **Memory Alignment Faults**: Accessing unaligned integers on strict architectures (e.g. SPARC/ARM).\n8. **Buffer Overflows**: Stack smashing via `gets`/`strcpy`.\n9. **Macro Multi-Evaluation**: `MAX(x++, y)` evaluates `x` twice.\n10. **Signal Safety**: Only async-signal-safe functions can be called inside signal handlers.\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "example.c",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    printf(\"=== 18: Master C Systems Drill ===\\n\");\n    printf(\"1. Pointer arithmetic & scaling\\n\");\n    printf(\"2. Heap fragmentation & free nullification\\n\");\n    printf(\"3. Struct packing & alignment padding\\n\");\n    printf(\"4. POSIX system call boundaries\\n\");\n    printf(\"🚀 You have completed the comprehensive C Mastery Track!\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "exercise",
            "type": "directory",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "starter.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "// TODO: Master Drill: Implement a memory-safe string duplicate function 'my_strdup'.\n"
              },
              {
                "name": "solution.c",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nchar* my_strdup(const char* s) {\n    if (!s) return NULL;\n    size_t len = strlen(s) + 1;\n    char* dup = (char*)malloc(len);\n    if (dup) {\n        memcpy(dup, s, len);\n    }\n    return dup;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    char* copy = my_strdup(\"Trak Systems Track\");\n    printf(\"Duplicated string: %s\\n\", copy);\n    free(copy);\n    printf(\"✔ my_strdup drill passed!\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}\n"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
